# Extracted assets / archives (built from user's ROM, never committed)
*.o2r
*.otr
/assets/extracted/
# Generated asset .c files carry real ROM content and are never committed. The matching
# headers under include/ are the opposite -- extern declarations and #defines, no game data --
# and they ARE tracked, because a fresh clone cannot build without them: 27 of the 65 come from
# Torch's `header` mode, which requires the ROM nobody else has. Same reasoning as
# port/gen/AssetBindings.c below. Regenerate the EK half with tools/gen_ek_assets.py, the rev0
# half with `gdx-extract header <rom> -s decomp -d include`.
/src/assets/
torch.hash.yml
# Generated asset bindings. These are generator OUTPUT plus hand-maintained rows on
# top, so they are committed rather than rebuilt: port/CMakeLists.txt requires the
# Ek* files unconditionally whenever GDX_EXPANSION_KIT is on (the default and the
# only supported configuration), and a fresh clone cannot configure without them.
# Regenerate with tools/gen_asset_bindings.py --out <scratch> and DIFF -- never
# straight over the tracked file, which would drop the hand-added rows.
/port/gen/*
!/port/gen/AssetBindings.c
!/port/gen/LinkStubs.c
!/port/gen/EkAssetBindings.c
!/port/gen/EkLinkStubs.c
!/port/gen/EkTranslatedOverrides.c
!/port/gen/EkTranslatedOverrides.h
!/port/gen/EkTranslatedStrings.c
!/port/gen/EkTranslatedStrings.h
# Copied to decomp-recipes/ by an UNCONDITIONAL POST_BUILD step (port/CMakeLists.txt
# ~556 for G-Diffuser, ~957 for the JP target), so a clone without it fails the build.
!/port/gen/ek_slice_manifest.txt
# Extraction goldens. These are __has_include-guarded in gdx_extract_launch.cpp, so a
# clone without them still builds -- but it silently falls back to placeholder
# expectations and every extraction is treated as unverifiable. Track them so a
# cloner gets the same validation the owner does.
!/port/gen/gdx_o2r_expected.h
!/port/gen/gdx_disk_expected.h
!/port/gen/gdx_ipl_expected.h
baserom*
*.z64
*.n64
*.ndd
*.z64dd

